      "message": "you could do this with reflection, something like (untested):\n\nv :\u003d reflect.ValueOf(a.properties.Dpi_variants)\nfor _, dpi :\u003d range dpiVariants {\n    f :\u003d v.FieldByName(proptools.FieldNameForProperty(dpi))\n    dpiApkMap[dpi] \u003d f.Interface().(*string)\n}\n\nYou could also create the Dpi_variants struct at runtime by making the type interface{} in AndroidAppImportProperties, using reflect.StructOf to create the a reflect.Type at runtime (inside a func init()?), then reflect.PtrTo to make it a pointer to the struct, and then in the factory assign a.properties.Dpi_variants \u003d reflect.Zero(runtimeCreatedType).  I think that would mean no hardcoded *dpi values, only a single list of valid values.",
